WEBVTT

00:33.990 --> 00:38.030
<b>And now for my report if I may.</b>

00:38.030 --> 00:42.200
<b>We just received word of the
Emperor of Earthwold's sudden passing.</b>

00:42.200 --> 00:44.500
<b></b>

00:44.500 --> 00:47.380
<b>"Crown Prince Wein Salema Arbalest,
Kingdom of Natra"
And there is now a power struggle
within the imperial palace.</b>

00:47.380 --> 00:51.300
<b>"Crown Prince Wein Salema Arbalest,
Kingdom of Natra"
The emperor's charisma is
what propelled the empire forward.</b>

00:51.300 --> 00:53.510
<b></b>

00:53.510 --> 00:55.010
<b>"Ninym Ralei, Aide to the Crown Prince,
Kingdom of Natra"
But the brighter the light,
the deeper the darkness that follows.</b>

00:55.010 --> 00:59.550
<b>"Ninym Ralei, Aide to the Crown Prince,
Kingdom of Natra"
It will be even darker if
they failed to name a successor.</b>

00:59.550 --> 01:04.390
<b>There is unrest within the empire
and the kingdoms surrounding us.</b>

01:04.390 --> 01:08.230
<b>However, we are...
Or should I say, here in Natra,</b>

01:08.230 --> 01:10.690
<b>we are graced with a beacon of hope.</b>

01:10.690 --> 01:14.190
<b>Prince Wein, that would be you,
Your Highness.</b>

01:15.110 --> 01:16.610
<b>But it's not just me.</b>

01:16.610 --> 01:19.700
<b>You liegemen who supported
my father all these years</b>

01:19.700 --> 01:22.450
<b>are also a beacon of hope.</b>

01:22.450 --> 01:23.620
<b>Your Highness.</b>

01:23.620 --> 01:26.290
<b>We are not worthy of such words.</b>

01:28.170 --> 01:31.670
<b>As long as we stand united
toward the same goal,</b>

01:31.670 --> 01:34.170
<b>there is no challenge we can't overcome.</b>

01:34.170 --> 01:38.720
<b>That earlier matter with the
imperial ambassador proves it.</b>

01:38.720 --> 01:41.220
<b>It is just as you say, Your Highness.</b>

01:41.220 --> 01:44.680
<b>Your Highness, what a
magnificent man you've become.</b>

01:44.680 --> 01:46.390
<b>Nothing else to report?</b>

01:46.390 --> 01:47.440
<b>Nothing more.</b>

01:47.440 --> 01:50.310
<b>Then I thank you. You're dismissed.</b>

01:50.310 --> 01:51.610
<b>Your Highness!</b>

02:06.290 --> 02:15.260
<b>I can't wait to sell off this kingdom!</b>

03:57.440 --> 04:00.740
<b>You're also a beacon of hope?</b>

04:00.740 --> 04:04.530
<b>As long as we stand united
toward the same goal?</b>

04:04.530 --> 04:06.160
<b>I didn't mean a word of it!</b>

04:06.160 --> 04:09.740
<b>No way in hell can I get this
kingdom out of the mess it's in!</b>

04:09.740 --> 04:13.750
<b>Ain't gonna happen! No way, no how!</b>

04:13.750 --> 04:19.000
<b>You shouldn't keep saying such things,
even if you're joking, Wein.</b>

04:19.000 --> 04:23.470
<b>I never said I was joking, Ninym!
I'm totally serious!</b>

04:23.470 --> 04:25.300
<b>That's even worse.</b>

04:25.300 --> 04:28.600
<b>You grow lazy the moment
you know no one's watching.</b>

04:28.600 --> 04:30.810
<b>You must try a little harder.</b>

04:30.810 --> 04:35.730
<b>Huh? What's with the poindexter act?</b>

04:35.730 --> 04:41.530
<b>Ninym, even you know how dirt poor
this kingdom is in every possible way.</b>

04:42.530 --> 04:46.110
<b>We're a petty kingdom
with no more than 500,000 subjects.</b>

04:46.110 --> 04:51.240
<b>And in the continent's far north,
spring is short, and winter is long.</b>

04:51.240 --> 04:54.910
<b>Plus, most of our territory
consists of barren rock and mountains.</b>

04:54.910 --> 04:57.630
<b>There's no money to invest
in domestic development,</b>

04:57.630 --> 05:00.420
<b>our meager resources mean
we can't raise capital,</b>

05:00.420 --> 05:03.340
<b>and we have no industries of value.</b>

05:03.340 --> 05:05.050
<b>And that's putting it lightly.</b>

05:05.050 --> 05:08.970
<b>We're a weak little kingdom that
could be wiped off the map in a flash.</b>

05:08.970 --> 05:12.720
<b>And now my old man's fallen ill,
and I gotta run things.</b>

05:12.720 --> 05:15.980
<b>I can't take it anymore!</b>

05:15.980 --> 05:20.480
<b>I can't wait to sell
this kingdom and disappear.</b>

05:20.480 --> 05:24.190
<b>But to do that,
first I gotta strengthen Natra.</b>

05:24.190 --> 05:28.990
<b>The greater a nation's value,
the higher the price it will fetch.</b>

05:28.990 --> 05:33.200
<b>That will affect how cushy
my retirement life will be!</b>

05:33.200 --> 05:36.500
<b>Yeah, yeah, I'm sick of hearing
that harebrained plan.</b>

05:36.500 --> 05:40.460
<b>There are other things
you should be worrying about.</b>

05:42.340 --> 05:43.710
<b></b>

05:43.710 --> 05:45.970
<b>"Princess Falanya Elk Arbalest,
Kingdom of Natra"
Dear Brother, sorry to bother
you when you're so busy.</b>

05:45.970 --> 05:48.300
<b>"Princess Falanya Elk Arbalest,
Kingdom of Natra"
Do you have a moment?</b>

05:48.300 --> 05:49.760
<b>Of course.</b>

05:52.140 --> 05:54.220
<b>Is something the matter, Falanya?</b>

05:54.220 --> 05:58.520
<b>I just saw Father and wished
to inform you of his condition.</b>

05:58.520 --> 05:59.560
<b>I see.</b>

05:59.560 --> 06:02.820
<b>Father is looking much better.</b>

06:02.820 --> 06:05.150
<b>He even felt ready to take a walk today.</b>

06:05.150 --> 06:07.070
<b>That's great news.</b>

06:07.070 --> 06:10.410
<b>But let's hold off on
that walk a bit longer.</b>

06:10.410 --> 06:11.870
<b>How come?</b>

06:11.870 --> 06:17.000
<b>The neighboring kingdom of Marden
is poised to invade Natra at any moment.</b>

06:17.000 --> 06:19.250
<b>What? Are you saying...?</b>

06:19.250 --> 06:20.880
<b>We're going to war.</b>

06:22.540 --> 06:25.760
<b>Marden was once on par with Natra</b>

06:25.760 --> 06:29.550
<b>until a newly discovered gold mine
allowed their kingdom to rapidly expand.</b>

06:29.550 --> 06:32.550
<b>However, their current king is unpopular.</b>

06:32.550 --> 06:34.350
<b>But you already know that.</b>

06:34.350 --> 06:35.350
<b>Yes.</b>

06:35.350 --> 06:38.310
<b>I learned he is served
by corrupt officials</b>

06:38.310 --> 06:43.980
<b>who ignore his failures and reaffirm
his belief that he's an enlightened ruler.</b>

06:43.980 --> 06:49.280
<b>He is creating a vicious cycle that
will drive his kingdom into the ground.</b>

06:49.280 --> 06:53.990
<b>That's why their king is looking
for an easy win to distract his people.</b>

06:53.990 --> 06:56.700
<b>And our kingdom fits the bill</b>

06:56.700 --> 07:00.420
<b>now that the imperial forces
that were stationed here are gone.</b>

07:00.420 --> 07:04.420
<b>But you won't let them do that, will you?</b>

07:04.420 --> 07:08.970
<b>I overheard the military officers
talking in the inner courtyard.</b>

07:08.970 --> 07:10.260
<b>What did they say?</b>

07:10.260 --> 07:14.430
<b>"Now is the time for the swords of
Natra to fulfill their appointed task!"</b>

07:14.430 --> 07:18.430
<b>And, "As liegemen, we must live up
to the prince's expectations."</b>

07:18.430 --> 07:19.310
<b>Stuff like that!</b>

07:19.310 --> 07:20.940
<b>Did they really?</b>

07:20.940 --> 07:23.690
<b>You heard them, too, right, Nanaki?</b>

07:24.520 --> 07:25.230
<b>"Nanaki Ralei, Falanya's Bodyguard"</b>

07:25.230 --> 07:27.940
<b>"Nanaki Ralei, Falanya's Bodyguard"
Yes, they wouldn't shut up.</b>

07:27.940 --> 07:31.740
<b>Oh no, are those idiots getting
all excited at the thought of battle?</b>

07:31.740 --> 07:33.620
<b>Are they raring to go?</b>

07:33.620 --> 07:37.870
<b>Do they have any idea how
expensive it is to wage war?!</b>

07:37.870 --> 07:39.500
<b>Brother?</b>

07:41.330 --> 07:45.250
<b>I'll pray for your victory.
That's all I can do.</b>

07:45.250 --> 07:47.590
<b>May you defeat our foes!</b>

07:47.590 --> 07:49.340
<b>Y-Yes, thanks.</b>

07:49.340 --> 07:54.180
<b>We'll launch a half-hearted attack
and then sue for peace.</b>

08:03.940 --> 08:08.320
<b>Natra's forces number
6,000 against Marden's 7,000.</b>

08:08.320 --> 08:10.150
<b>Your Highness.</b>

08:10.150 --> 08:12.950
<b>Both armies are arrayed on the field.</b>

08:12.950 --> 08:15.570
<b>Now we wait for the battle to begin.</b>

08:15.570 --> 08:16.830
<b>Yes, Your Highness.</b>

08:16.830 --> 08:19.120
<b>And I was hoping</b>

08:19.120 --> 08:22.040
<b>you might have some words for the troops.</b>

08:22.040 --> 08:25.170
<b>Battles wear down more
than a soldier's body.</b>

08:25.170 --> 08:27.920
<b>They also take a toll on his soul.</b>

08:27.920 --> 08:32.970
<b>Would you not give them a
few words to boost their morale?</b>

08:32.970 --> 08:35.430
<b>Though they've been trained by the empire,</b>

08:35.430 --> 08:39.470
<b>their tension is palpable,
for this is their first real battle.</b>

08:42.850 --> 08:45.560
<b>Torace of Heinoy.</b>

08:45.560 --> 08:47.940
<b>Your spear is upside down.</b>

08:49.400 --> 08:53.070
<b>Forgive me, Your Highness!</b>

08:53.070 --> 08:55.070
<b>Karlmann, Patess,</b>

08:55.070 --> 08:56.570
<b>Livi, Logli.</b>

08:56.570 --> 08:58.410
<b>It's not that funny.</b>

08:58.410 --> 09:00.200
<b>Yes, Your Highness!</b>

09:01.080 --> 09:04.160
<b>That eased the tension a bit.</b>

09:05.670 --> 09:10.420
<b>Until this day, Natra's army has
been looked down on as weak.</b>

09:10.420 --> 09:13.670
<b>It may have been true at one time.</b>

09:13.670 --> 09:17.720
<b>Marden's army likely
looks down on us, too.</b>

09:17.720 --> 09:19.800
<b>But I know the truth.</b>

09:19.800 --> 09:23.680
<b>You have survived
the most grueling training.</b>

09:23.680 --> 09:28.770
<b>I know that you possess a noble
courage that is beyond compare.</b>

09:28.770 --> 09:35.990
<b>And I know that as you face our invaders,
a flame imperishable burns in your hearts.</b>

09:35.990 --> 09:42.200
<b>Therefore, you can no longer
be seen as weak by any measure.</b>

09:43.700 --> 09:45.910
<b>Now prove it in battle!</b>

09:45.910 --> 09:48.790
<b>Show them that we are
the dragon of the north!</b>

09:48.790 --> 09:53.420
<b>Let it resound across the continent!
We are the most formidable force of all!</b>

09:53.420 --> 09:57.930
<b>Today is the day we fight
and rewrite history!</b>

10:05.100 --> 10:07.020
<b>That was magnificent.</b>

10:07.020 --> 10:11.480
<b>At least they won't be so nervous
that they lose hold of their weapons.</b>

10:11.480 --> 10:16.400
<b>Did you plant those soldiers
you addressed by name?</b>

10:16.400 --> 10:19.740
<b>Don't be silly. I was winging it.</b>

10:19.740 --> 10:22.780
<b>We're not an empire with
hundreds of thousands of troops.</b>

10:22.780 --> 10:27.580
<b>Natra only has about 10,000
if you add them all up.</b>

10:43.180 --> 10:46.640
<b>Hear me, brave warriors of Marden!</b>

10:46.640 --> 10:49.600
<b>Natra's troops are
but lowly foot soldiers!</b>

10:49.600 --> 10:51.860
<b>They mistake recklessness for courage</b>

10:51.860 --> 10:56.070
<b>and are now trying to thwart
our advance like the fools they are.</b>

10:56.070 --> 10:59.650
<b>But there is no way in hell
these northern peasants</b>

10:59.650 --> 11:03.410
<b>can defeat our army of elite troops!</b>

11:04.950 --> 11:06.410
<b>Trample them underfoot!</b>

11:06.410 --> 11:10.580
<b>Stain this wasteland red with their blood!</b>

11:13.210 --> 11:15.670
<b>Stand ready, men!</b>

11:19.220 --> 11:20.970
<b>Ready...</b>

11:20.970 --> 11:22.930
<b>Attack!</b>

11:33.400 --> 11:35.270
<b>I have a report, Your Highness!</b>

11:35.270 --> 11:38.940
<b>Marden's troops are in a
center-heavy formation!</b>

11:38.940 --> 11:44.320
<b>We'll break through their center,
then turn and crush them from behind!</b>

11:44.320 --> 11:46.910
<b>In that case, we'll stand our ground!</b>

11:46.910 --> 11:49.120
<b>They'll break upon our defensive line.</b>

11:49.120 --> 11:52.170
<b>The Mardenian army
won't know what hit them!</b>

12:01.590 --> 12:03.800
<b>Hey, hey, hey!</b>

12:03.800 --> 12:06.300
<b>W-Wait a second. What is happening?</b>

12:06.300 --> 12:10.100
<b>General Urgio! Our left flank
is requesting reinforcements!</b>

12:10.100 --> 12:14.270
<b>Sir! Sanse Company was decimated!
Tology Company is moving to fill the void!</b>

12:14.270 --> 12:17.230
<b>General! Our right flank
is in dire straits, too!</b>

12:17.230 --> 12:21.610
<b>What the hell?! How can these
Natran troops be so formidable?!</b>

12:21.610 --> 12:25.200
<b>How can Marden be so weak?!</b>

12:25.200 --> 12:29.200
<b>What is going on? How can
we possibly be kicking their butt?</b>

12:34.330 --> 12:37.790
<b>What's with Marden's tactics?
It's not a schoolyard brawl!</b>

12:38.210 --> 12:41.170
<b>Meanwhile, our troops are dominating.</b>

12:41.170 --> 12:43.630
<b>Is there a problem, Your Highness?</b>

12:43.630 --> 12:47.680
<b>No. It's just I'm surprised by how
fiercely our troops are fighting.</b>

12:47.680 --> 12:51.680
<b>Has it all not gone as you planned,
Your Highness?</b>

12:51.680 --> 12:57.480
<b>I remember that day you met
with the imperial ambassador.</b>

12:57.480 --> 12:59.070
<b>Ambassador Brandel.</b>

12:59.070 --> 13:03.820
<b>"Ambassador Fisch Brandel,
Empire of Earthwold"
I view maintaining relations
with the empire as my top priority.</b>

13:03.820 --> 13:06.280
<b>As such, should we not bridge the divide</b>

13:06.280 --> 13:10.580
<b>between the Imperial Army
and Natra's Royal Army?</b>

13:10.580 --> 13:12.120
<b>I concur, Your Highness.</b>

13:12.120 --> 13:13.580
<b>What I propose is this.</b>

13:13.580 --> 13:19.630
<b>Would you not provide the Imperial Army's
expertise and funding to our Royal Army?</b>

13:20.840 --> 13:26.180
<b>Who would ever believe
they would accept such a request?</b>

13:26.180 --> 13:29.930
<b>But Ambassador Brandel <i>did </i>accept it.</b>

13:29.930 --> 13:35.230
<b>That means we've adopted the methods of
the continent's greatest military force.</b>

13:35.230 --> 13:39.110
<b>And now that our military has
tapped the empire's abundant capital,</b>

13:39.110 --> 13:41.650
<b>it's grown more powerful before our eyes.</b>

13:41.650 --> 13:43.780
<b>Natra's army is more than a match</b>

13:43.780 --> 13:48.780
<b>for any petty kingdom that has
only experienced limited skirmishes.</b>

13:48.780 --> 13:54.290
<b>Ideally, Marden will cut
their losses and run, but...</b>

13:54.290 --> 13:58.000
<b>Your Highness! The center
of our line is under pressure!</b>

13:59.210 --> 14:02.000
<b>The morale of our forces
is starting to fray.</b>

14:02.000 --> 14:03.760
<b>Crap!</b>

14:03.760 --> 14:06.010
<b>After all that training?</b>

14:06.010 --> 14:09.300
<b>Even after rigorous training
and your inspiring words,</b>

14:09.300 --> 14:14.850
<b>Natra's troops are not mentally
prepared for a real battlefield.</b>

14:14.850 --> 14:20.730
<b>The chill air, splattering blood,
and wanton slaughter consume them.</b>

14:22.520 --> 14:26.030
<b>The tide turns against us.</b>

14:26.860 --> 14:29.820
<b>Please don't notice.</b>

14:33.370 --> 14:36.580
<b>Natra's forces are
no longer pressing the attack.</b>

14:36.580 --> 14:39.960
<b>Their strength is but a facade.</b>

14:39.960 --> 14:44.090
<b>Order the commanders of
both flanks to enter the fray</b>

14:44.090 --> 14:47.090
<b>and stop the enemy dead in their tracks!</b>

14:47.090 --> 14:50.640
<b>And have our forces in
the center reform their lines!</b>

14:50.640 --> 14:52.800
<b>We strike once they are ready!</b>

14:52.800 --> 14:55.060
<b>What's the target?</b>

14:55.640 --> 14:59.850
<b>The head of their leader!</b>

15:02.480 --> 15:03.940
<b>Oh, crap!</b>

15:03.940 --> 15:05.690
<b>He noticed.</b>

15:05.690 --> 15:08.360
<b>Your Highness, we must fall back now.</b>

15:08.360 --> 15:10.410
<b>I know.</b>

15:10.410 --> 15:13.660
<b>General! They're fleeing from their camp!</b>

15:13.660 --> 15:18.080
<b>Pathetic. It's better
to fall bravely in battle.</b>

15:18.710 --> 15:22.460
<b>Take them from behind
before they can hide in the hills.</b>

15:24.750 --> 15:27.800
<b>Damnit. How did this happen?</b>

15:28.170 --> 15:33.640
<b>Quickly, men, turnabout!</b>

15:33.640 --> 15:36.010
<b>They've accepted their fate!</b>

15:43.520 --> 15:48.400
<b>Archers, loose!</b>

15:48.400 --> 15:51.860
<b>This is looking like a complete victory!</b>

15:57.080 --> 15:58.620
<b>Wh-What's this?!</b>

15:58.620 --> 16:01.620
<b>An ambush?!</b>

16:01.620 --> 16:03.000
<b>They're attacking!</b>

16:03.000 --> 16:05.920
<b>Defend General Urgio with your lives!</b>

16:05.920 --> 16:07.210
<b>Pathetic.</b>

16:18.430 --> 16:19.970
<b>Why you...!</b>

16:20.980 --> 16:22.980
<b>You're the general, I take it?</b>

16:22.980 --> 16:27.570
<b>Surrender now, and you
may survive with prompt treatment.</b>

16:27.570 --> 16:30.940
<b>Surrender? Surrender, you say?</b>

16:30.940 --> 16:32.320
<b>To hell with that!</b>

16:32.320 --> 16:34.320
<b>I'm the general of Marden's army!</b>

16:34.320 --> 16:39.790
<b>I'm not gonna surrender to some woman,
and a lowly, dirty Flahm at that!</b>

16:39.790 --> 16:41.120
<b>So be it.</b>

16:46.420 --> 16:49.750
<b>Take his head and
raise it high for all to see.</b>

16:49.750 --> 16:54.590
<b>And see that his last words
are never heard again.</b>

16:54.590 --> 16:56.050
<b>Yes, ma'am.</b>

16:56.050 --> 17:00.560
<b>The enemy general died in
silence as far as I'm concerned.</b>

17:17.570 --> 17:20.490
<b>This battle's pretty much over.</b>

17:20.490 --> 17:21.870
<b>Yes, indeed.</b>

17:21.870 --> 17:26.460
<b>Now what the hell am I supposed to do?</b>

17:28.210 --> 17:31.500
<b>Now that we've crushed
the Mardenian invaders,</b>

17:31.500 --> 17:34.760
<b>Eastern Marden is utterly exposed!</b>

17:34.760 --> 17:38.800
<b>We should turn the tables
and invade at once!</b>

17:38.800 --> 17:43.350
<b>We could carve off a
large chunk of their territory!</b>

17:43.350 --> 17:44.640
<b>I agree.</b>

17:44.640 --> 17:49.400
<b>Our swift victory means we still
have plenty of troops and supplies.</b>

17:49.400 --> 17:50.270
<b>Your Highness!</b>

17:50.270 --> 17:53.230
<b>What is your command?!</b>

17:53.230 --> 17:54.990
<b>I can't believe this!</b>

17:54.990 --> 18:00.160
<b>Do they have any idea how risky it is
to invade without carefully planning?!</b>

18:00.160 --> 18:02.950
<b>But how can I possibly say that now?</b>

18:02.950 --> 18:05.710
<b>Now that we've utterly
crushed Marden's army,</b>

18:05.710 --> 18:11.500
<b>weak-kneed words will cause my generals'
loyalty to crash down like an avalanche.</b>

18:11.500 --> 18:15.630
<b>And that can only end in a coup d'etat!</b>

18:15.630 --> 18:19.970
<b>I didn't want to do this,
but I've got no choice.</b>

18:19.970 --> 18:22.220
<b>I hear what you're saying.</b>

18:22.220 --> 18:28.060
<b>You're correct in saying our great victory
has put tremendous momentum behind us.</b>

18:28.980 --> 18:32.440
<b>That is why I propose this.</b>

18:32.440 --> 18:36.110
<b>As you know, ours is a barren,
unprosperous land.</b>

18:36.110 --> 18:40.160
<b>But the same can be said of Marden.</b>

18:40.160 --> 18:43.370
<b>And its eastern region
has few strategic points.</b>

18:43.370 --> 18:47.960
<b>Based on our current troop strength
and places within our grasp,</b>

18:47.960 --> 18:51.710
<b>there <i>is </i>a location worth taking.</b>

18:51.710 --> 18:53.500
<b>The Jilaat Gold Mine.</b>

18:53.500 --> 18:56.880
<b>If we're to capture anything,
it should be that.</b>

18:58.590 --> 19:01.180
<b>Yes! That's the reaction I wanted.</b>

19:01.180 --> 19:04.430
<b>After all, targeting
their gold mine is crazy talk!</b>

19:04.430 --> 19:06.930
<b>No matter how much strategic value it has,</b>

19:06.930 --> 19:12.690
<b>attacking without much intel
and with troops weary from battle</b>

19:12.690 --> 19:16.610
<b>would be fruitless, futile, feckless.</b>

19:16.610 --> 19:19.490
<b>But it has stoked a serious debate.</b>

19:19.490 --> 19:23.160
<b>The gold mine is impossible,
so they need another target.</b>

19:23.160 --> 19:26.290
<b>But where? Does Eastern Marden
have another location</b>

19:26.290 --> 19:28.540
<b>with the strategic value of the mine?</b>

19:28.540 --> 19:30.540
<b>No! No, it doesn't!</b>

19:30.540 --> 19:32.960
<b>There are no other targets of value!</b>

19:32.960 --> 19:35.340
<b>The other possibilities are worthless.</b>

19:35.340 --> 19:40.180
<b>The moment they realize that,
their thirst for conquests will vanish.</b>

19:40.180 --> 19:43.800
<b>They may think a bit less of me
for making a ludicrous proposal,</b>

19:43.800 --> 19:45.260
<b>but I'm used to it!</b>

19:45.260 --> 19:49.600
<b>And it'll be totally worth it
if they decide to withdraw!</b>

19:49.600 --> 19:50.480
<b>Your Highness.</b>

19:50.480 --> 19:53.310
<b>Here it comes!</b>

19:53.310 --> 19:56.690
<b>Well? Tell me my proposal is crazy talk.</b>

19:56.690 --> 20:00.280
<b>They want to tell me how reckless it is,
but they don't know how.</b>

20:00.280 --> 20:03.280
<b>I gotta think of a way for
my officers to preserve their honor</b>

20:03.280 --> 20:07.490
<b>by acting like their wisdom
struck deep into my soul.</b>

20:07.490 --> 20:09.120
<b>If I do that, everything will be--</b>

20:09.120 --> 20:12.710
<b>I am in awe of your intellect.</b>

20:12.710 --> 20:13.670
<b>What?!</b>

20:13.670 --> 20:15.960
<b>It is just as you say, Your Highness.</b>

20:15.960 --> 20:19.170
<b>The Jilaat Gold Mine
is the only target of worth!</b>

20:19.170 --> 20:21.130
<b>This is, indeed, a surprise.</b>

20:21.130 --> 20:23.800
<b>I can hardly believe that your Highness</b>

20:23.800 --> 20:27.350
<b>knew of our long-standing plan
to take the gold mine.</b>

20:27.350 --> 20:29.640
<b>I'm absolutely speechless.</b>

20:29.640 --> 20:32.350
<b>Wait, what?!</b>

20:32.350 --> 20:34.770
<b>While we were celebrating our victory,</b>

20:34.770 --> 20:38.780
<b>Your Highness must have been
studying the feasibility of our plan.</b>

20:38.780 --> 20:41.530
<b>I'm humbled by your foresight.</b>

20:42.610 --> 20:45.620
<b>Your Highness, we'll set out
at once upon your command!</b>

20:45.620 --> 20:48.540
<b>Let us strike the gold mine
while the iron's hot!</b>

20:48.540 --> 20:50.200
<b>--Your Highness!
--Your Highness!</b>

20:50.200 --> 20:51.870
<b>Your Highness!</b>

20:55.040 --> 20:57.090
<b>Ninym, help.</b>

20:57.090 --> 20:59.130
<b>Sorry. Nothing I can do.</b>

21:04.220 --> 21:07.720
<b>The invasion of Marden is a done deal.</b>

21:07.720 --> 21:12.390
<b>I could've nixed the plan if
our army hadn't won by a landslide.</b>

21:13.100 --> 21:14.980
<b>So what now, Wein?</b>

21:14.980 --> 21:17.980
<b>I don't wanna think about it.
I can't even.</b>

21:17.980 --> 21:19.980
<b>You know that's not an option.</b>

21:19.980 --> 21:21.190
<b>It's not?</b>

21:21.190 --> 21:22.320
<b>No, it's not.</b>

21:22.320 --> 21:26.870
<b>Okay, I'll think of something
if you meow like a cat.</b>

21:26.870 --> 21:28.370
<b>Well, come on then!</b>

21:28.370 --> 21:30.620
<b>Cat got your tongue, Ninym?</b>

21:30.620 --> 21:33.000
<b>Has curiosity killed your inner cat?</b>

21:33.000 --> 21:36.420
<b>Too proud to channel your inner feline?</b>

21:37.460 --> 21:40.340
<b>Fine. Meow.</b>

21:41.880 --> 21:43.880
<b>So, what's the plan?</b>

21:43.880 --> 21:45.010
<b>Let's see.</b>

21:45.010 --> 21:49.350
<b>We should start by verifying
the intel on the mine's defenses.</b>

21:49.350 --> 21:51.810
<b>Then we should reassess our supply lines</b>

21:51.810 --> 21:54.560
<b>and do our best to maintain troop morale.</b>

21:54.560 --> 21:58.770
<b>We can take the mine before Marden
can mount an adequate defense.</b>

21:58.770 --> 22:03.820
<b>But that's all easier said than done.</b>

22:03.820 --> 22:05.200
<b>Meow.</b>

22:05.200 --> 22:09.070
<b>I know. It's back-to-back battles
after the Polta Highlands.</b>

22:09.070 --> 22:11.700
<b>We're bound to stumble somewhere.</b>

22:11.700 --> 22:16.710
<b>But that stumble is just what we
need to convince our army to withdraw.</b>

22:17.330 --> 22:20.210
<b>Now we wait for that to happen.</b>

22:20.210 --> 22:22.800
<b>Right.</b>

22:22.800 --> 22:24.260
<b>Meow.</b>

22:26.720 --> 22:29.220
<b>Well, that didn't work.</b>

22:29.220 --> 22:31.260
<b>We actually took the mine.</b>

22:31.260 --> 22:35.310
<b>We actually took it.</b>

22:35.310 --> 22:37.890
<b>Come on, meow for me.</b>

22:37.890 --> 22:39.980
<b>I'm so over that.</b>
